A||||6||Fiero*101||Why does my engine get so hot?||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero*101||08-14-2001||10:18 AM||||Ok i only drive a little bit and i dont go very far and it gets really hot<P><BR>any ideas<P>keep in mind it has all new coolent in it and it has a new thermostat.<P>and i was just wondering if any body else has this problem.<P>thanks<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000001||hyhy4u||08-14-2001||11:47 AM||||How hot is really hot???<BR>Does it overheat or just get really hot??, lol<BR>Did it do this before you changed the coolent and thermostat??<P>Thinking we need a little more info<P>-Jason<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero*101||08-14-2001||03:58 PM||||it doesnt overheat. and yes it over heated before i got the new thermostat and coolant in it<P>but it still gets hotter then my other vehicles(sp?)<P>do they all do that?<P>i dont know how hot it is but my trunk and my vents are like sometimes to hot to touch and i was just wondering why they get so hot<P>and im guessing its b/c there so close to the engine.<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||08-14-2001||04:07 PM||||Are you talkin 220* hot or almost to the red on the temp gauge hot?  If it is 220 hot...that is norman operating tempurature for the engines.  If it is way hotter than that it could be a bad thermostat.  Good way to check the thermostat is to boil some water on the stove...get it to the rating on your stat (180* stat= 180* water) and put the thermostat in.  It should begin to open at the tempurature it is rated at.  <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-14-2001||04:24 PM||||The car runs hot because it burns gasoline.  The exhaust gases are hot, the engine gets hot, the exhaust manifold gets hot, the muffler gets hot and it is all crammed into a small space.<P>If the waterpump is working, the radiator is free flowing and the thermostate is working and the temperature guage shows 195-220 degrees or so, the car is running as expected.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-14-2001||07:18 PM||||the rear hood grills on my Ferrari kit get hot enough to make hamburgers and eggs. so you cant judge how hot it is by touch. If gauge is around 220 or less-your normal. at nite (V6 anyway) get in the dark and open engine cover and look at your exhaust pipes.<BR>thats how hot it gets.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero*101||08-14-2001||11:40 PM||||Thank you i was getting worried this Fiero stuff is new to me but im learing and loving evry min of it<P>Thanks again<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
